@.str.55 = private unnamed_addr constant [1054 x i8] c"Compute the convex hull of a point cloud using qhull. This runs on the CPU.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    joggle_inputs (bool, default=False): Handle precision problems by\0A        randomly perturbing the input data. Set to True if perturbing the input\0A        iis acceptable but you need convex simplicial output. If False,\0A        neighboring facets may be merged in case of precision problems. See\0A        `QHull docs <http://www.qhull.org/html/qh-impre.htm#joggle`__ for more\0A        details.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    TriangleMesh representing the convexh hull. This contains an\0A    extra vertex property \22point_indices\22 that contains the index of the\0A    corresponding vertex in the original mesh.\0A\0AExample:\0A    We will load the Stanford Bunny dataset, compute and display it's convex hull::\0A\0A        bunny = o3d.data.BunnyMesh()\0A        mesh = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.from_legacy(o3d.io.read_triangle_mesh(bunny.path))\0A        hull = mesh.compute_convex_hull()\0A        o3d.visualization.draw([{'name': 'bunny', 'geometry': mesh}, {'name': 'convex hull', 'geometry': hull}])\0A\00", align 1
