@.str.69 = private unnamed_addr constant [799 x i8] c"Returns a new triangle mesh clipped with the plane.\0A\0AThis method clips the triangle mesh with the specified plane.\0AParts of the mesh on the positive side of the plane will be kept and triangles\0Aintersected by the plane will be cut.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    point (open3d.core.Tensor): A point on the plane.\0A\0A    normal (open3d.core.Tensor): The normal of the plane. The normal points to\0A        the positive side of the plane for which the geometry will be kept.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    New triangle mesh clipped with the plane.\0A\0A\0AThis example shows how to create a hemisphere from a sphere::\0A\0A    import open3d as o3d\0A\0A    sphere = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.from_legacy(o3d.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_sphere())\0A    hemisphere = sphere.clip_plane(point=[0,0,0], normal=[1,0,0])\0A\0A    o3d.visualization.draw(hemisphere)\0A\00", align 1
