@.str.72 = private unnamed_addr constant [881 x i8] c"Returns a line set with the contour slices defined by the plane and values.\0A\0AThis method generates slices as LineSet from the mesh at specific contour\0Avalues with respect to a plane.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    point (open3d.core.Tensor): A point on the plane.\0A    normal (open3d.core.Tensor): The normal of the plane.\0A    contour_values (list): A list of contour values at which slices will be\0A        generated. The value describes the signed distance to the plane.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    LineSet with the extracted contours.\0A\0A\0AThis example shows how to create a hemisphere from a sphere::\0A\0A    import open3d as o3d\0A    import numpy as np\0A\0A    bunny = o3d.data.BunnyMesh()\0A    mesh = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.from_legacy(o3d.io.read_triangle_mesh(bunny.path))\0A    contours = mesh.slice_plane([0,0,0], [0,1,0], np.linspace(0,0.2))\0A    o3d.visualization.draw([{'name': 'bunny', 'geometry': contours}])\0A\0A\00", align 1
