@.str.161 = private unnamed_addr constant [1711 x i8] c"Create a mesh from a 3D scalar field (volume) by computing the\0Aisosurface.\0A\0AThis method uses the Flying Edges dual contouring method that computes the\0Aisosurface similar to Marching Cubes. The center of the first voxel of the\0Avolume is at the origin (0,0,0). The center of the voxel at index [z,y,x]\0Awill be at (x,y,z).\0A\0AArgs:\0A    volume (open3d.core.Tensor): 3D tensor with the volume.\0A    contour_values (list): A list of contour values at which isosurfaces will\0A        be generated. The default value is 0.\0A    device (o3d.core.Device): The device for the returned mesh.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    A TriangleMesh with the extracted isosurfaces.\0A\0A\0AThis example shows how to create a sphere from a volume::\0A\0A    import open3d as o3d\0A    import numpy as np\0A\0A    grid_coords = np.stack(np.meshgrid(*3*[np.linspace(-1,1,num=64)], indexing='ij'), axis=-1)\0A    vol = 0.5 - np.linalg.norm(grid_coords, axis=-1)\0A    mesh = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_isosurfaces(vol)\0A    o3d.visualization.draw(mesh)\0A\0A\0AThis example shows how to convert a mesh to a signed distance field (SDF) and back to a mesh::\0A\0A    import open3d as o3d\0A    import numpy as np\0A\0A    mesh1 = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_torus()\0A    grid_coords = np.stack(np.meshgrid(*3*[np.linspace(-2,2,num=64, dtype=np.float32)], indexing='ij'), axis=-1)\0A\0A    scene = o3d.t.geometry.RaycastingScene()\0A    scene.add_triangles(mesh1)\0A    sdf = scene.compute_signed_distance(grid_coords)\0A    mesh2 = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_isosurfaces(sdf)\0A\0A    # Flip the triangle orientation for SDFs with negative values as \22inside\22 and positive values as \22outside\22\0A    mesh2.triangle.indices = mesh2.triangle.indices[:,[2,1,0]]\0A\0A    o3d.visualization.draw(mesh2)\0A\0A\00", align 1
